msgctxt "188"
msgid "(Kashiwagi-san...)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "200"
msgid "Aniki."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "212"
msgid "What's up?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "224"
msgid "What kinda guy was Kashiwagi-san?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "248"
msgid ""
"Kashiwagi-san, he... he knew what my adoptive father,\r\n"
"Kazama-san, stood for. Kept the Kazama Family legacy alive\r\n"
"when he took over as their second patriarch."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "260"
msgid "Honestly, Kashiwagi-san was..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "272"
msgid "Great at leading from the shadows."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "284"
msgid ""
"He didn't really like being the center of attention, but I\r\n"
"can't tell you how many times he saved my life."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "296"
msgid ""
"It was also thanks to Kashiwagi-san that Daigo was able to\r\n"
"take control of the Tojo despite being so young. He was a\r\n"
"priceless asset to the clan."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "308"
msgid "Wow. I always figured he was amazin', but never knew just how much."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "320"
msgid "Great at hiding in the shadows."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "332"
msgid "Huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "344"
msgid ""
"It's almost like he let others take the spotlight while he\r\n"
"sat back and watched. Makes sense with how many big\r\n"
"personalities there are in the Tojo Clan."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "356"
msgid ""
"But he was still a leader, right? Pullin' strings, plannin'\r\n"
"plans. I bet the guy had his finger in all sortsa pies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "368"
msgid "Yeah, I guess you're right."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "380"
msgid ""
"I'm sure I'm right! How else would he have ended up captain\r\n"
"of one of the biggest yakuza organizations in the country!?\r\n"
"He really must've been amazin'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "392"
msgid "Amazing? Yeah. Yeah, I guess so. I was especially in awe of..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "404"
msgid "I was especially in awe of how level-headed he was."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "416"
msgid ""
"I think that's why Kazama-san trusted him so much.\r\n"
"Kashiwagi-san really lived up to that trust, too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "428"
msgid ""
"He always kept tensions between families from boiling over,\r\n"
"though of course that made some of the patriarchs think he\r\n"
"was soft. Too soft to lead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "440"
msgid "That's a reputation you wanna avoid in this line of work."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "452"
msgid ""
"Even so, you can't just fight people for no reason. You have\r\n"
"to choose your battles, and Kashiwagi-san knew how to do\r\n"
"that better than anyone."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "464"
msgid "Whoa. You musta really respected him, Aniki."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "476"
msgid "I was especially in awe of how much he loved cold noodles."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "488"
msgid "Huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "500"
msgid ""
"We always used to go get yakiniku together when I was young,\r\n"
"and he'd order cold noodles every time, without fail."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "512"
msgid ""
"He'd get so worked up if they were out, too. Sometimes he'd\r\n"
"even send me to the store to get ingredients so the shop could make more."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "524"
msgid "You were an errand boy, Aniki?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "536"
msgid ""
"There's nothing strange about doing what the boss says.\r\n"
"Especially when you're just starting out."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "548"
msgid "No, of course it's not strange! Definitely not, haha..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "560"
msgid ""
"Listen, Rikiya. You don't understand what Kashiwagi-san was\r\n"
"like when he couldn't get his noodles. It was terrifying!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "572"
msgid "All right, all right! Don't blow a fuse over there, Aniki."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "584"
msgid ""
"...Sorry. I will say, though. The only time I ever saw\r\n"
"Kashiwagi-san get upset like that was when he couldn't get\r\n"
"his noodles."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "596"
msgid ""
"Huh, never would've guessed. Kinda scary to think about,\r\n"
"but I suppose everyone's got somethin' they go wild for."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "704"
msgid "We should probably get going, Rikiya."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "716"
msgid "Mhm."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "728"
msgid "Anywhere else you had in mind?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "740"
msgid "I dunno, all this talking kinda made me sad."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "752"
msgid ""
"Hey, why don't we go to one of those bikini bars I've heard\r\n"
"about!? Whaddya say, Aniki?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "764"
msgid "...Seriously?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "776"
msgid ""
"Hell yeah! You can't expect me to leave Tokyo without first\r\n"
"gettin' a little taste of the ladies! But, uh... I can go by myself if you "
"really want."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "788"
msgid ""
"That might be for the best. Sorry... I'm not really feeling\r\n"
"up to it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "800"
msgid "Figured. My bad, Aniki. I was just tryin' to cheer you up."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "812"
msgid "Don't worry, Rikiya. I'm okay. Go have some fun."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "824"
msgid "But..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "836"
msgid "Just go. And Rikiya...? Thanks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "848"
msgid ""
"What, that? It was nothin', Aniki! Just wish I could've been\r\n"
"more help, ya know?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "860"
msgid "Anyway, guess I'll get goin'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "872"
msgid "Think you can manage on your own?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "884"
msgid "Oh, totally! I got a pretty good feel for the layout by now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "896"
msgid ""
"Heh, if you say so. By the way, there's a bar called New\r\n"
"Serena over on Tenkaichi Street that we're gonna be using\r\n"
"as our base of operations."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "908"
msgid ""
"Head there when you're done wandering. And feel free to give\r\n"
"me a call if you have trouble finding it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "920"
msgid "Will do. Catch ya later, Aniki!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "932"
msgid ""
"By the way, Aniki. Here's a little thank you for showin' me\r\n"
"around."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "968"
msgid "You got a <Color:8>Zero Jewel<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "992"
msgid "You got a <Color:8>1-1-1 Card<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1016"
msgid "You got a <Color:8>Silver Plate<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1040"
msgid "You got a <Color:8>Toughness Infinity<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1064"
msgid "Well, later!"
msgstr ""

